Electron uVT validation
=======================

This example is intentionally split into two parallel layers.

Toy regression
--------------

Directory:

- ``toy/``

This is the LAMMPS-side quadratic toy-model regression for classical uVT.
It checks the generic fix integration, the thermostat/potentiostat coupling,
and restart continuity against an analytic equilibrium.

Real-system validation
----------------------

Directory:

- ``volmer/``

This is a separate template for a real Volmer / PCET-style validation at one
chosen state, typically an initial state. It is intentionally kept apart from
the toy regression so the two layers do not get mixed together.
The first recommended check uses one fixed ``mu`` value to verify that the
constant-potential implementation is working at all.
The Volmer layer keeps the same light layout as the toy layer: input scripts
plus a notebook for analysis and plots.

The key contract is still the same in both layers:

- ``fix uvt`` consumes ``dedn``
- the actual source of ``dE/dN`` can come from a variable, compute, fix,
  or a model-specific helper

Running
-------

From the LAMMPS root directory:

- ``./build-unified/lmp -in examples/electron-uvt/toy/in.electron_uvt``
- ``./build-unified/lmp -in examples/electron-uvt/toy/in.electron_uvt_restart``
- ``./build-unified/lmp -in examples/electron-uvt/volmer/in.volmer``

If you prefer to run from inside ``toy/`` or ``volmer/``, use:

- ``../../../build-unified/lmp``
